>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="cost">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does a bathroom installation cost in Liverpool?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full bathroom with us starts from £4,995, supplied and fitted, including VAT. A bath to shower conversion starts from £2,395.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Price, inc VAT</th><th>Typical time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Cloakroom or WC</strong></td><td>from £2,495</td><td>A few days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Bath to shower conversion</strong></td><td>from £2,395</td><td>2 to 3 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>En-suite shower room</strong></td><td>from £4,495</td><td>Set out in your quote</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Full bathroom, supplied and fitted</strong></td><td>from £4,995</td><td>5 to 7 working days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Labour-only full refit (your own suite)</strong></td><td>from £2,750</td><td>5 to 7 working days</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>What changes the price?</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Moving things.</strong> Moving a toilet or waste costs more than keeping it in place.</li>
        <li><strong>The suite and tiles you pick.</strong> Premium ranges cost more.</li>
        <li><strong>Room size.</strong> More wall and floor means more tiling.</li>
        <li><strong>What is under the old bath.</strong> Rotten boards or old pipes are priced before we fix them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Only need a new shower? See our <a href="/showers-liverpool">shower installation</a> prices, from £375 fitted.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in a bathroom installation?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Everything from the strip-out to the final clean. Your quote lists what is in and what is not, so you can compare it fairly.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Strip-out and disposal.</strong> The old suite and tiles leave with us. No skip needed.</li>
        <li><strong>All plumbing.</strong> New supply and waste pipes, run and clipped properly.</li>
        <li><strong>Tiling.</strong> James's team does the tiling. Or we fit waterproof wall panels if you prefer.</li>
        <li><strong>The suite.</strong> Bath or shower, toilet, basin, taps and valves, fitted and sealed.</li>
        <li><strong>Electrics.</strong> Lights, extractor fans and electric shower circuits by our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Making good.</strong> We test every joint, seal everything and clean before we leave.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Tiles:</strong> we can supply them, or you can buy your own. <strong>Suite:</strong> the same. If you buy your own suite, the labour-only price is from £2,750.</p>
      <p></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="which">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Start with what is wrong with the room now. If only the bath is the problem, a conversion may be all you need.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Bath to shower, from £2,395</h3>
          <p>Best if you rarely use the bath, or getting in and out is hard. Quick, with 2 to 3 days on site.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Full bathroom, from £4,995</h3>
          <p>Best if the suite, tiles and pipes are all tired. One job, and the whole room is new.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>En-suite, from £4,495</h3>
          <p>A shower room off a bedroom. Good for busy homes where one bathroom is not enough.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Cloakroom or WC, from £2,495</h3>
          <p>A toilet and basin downstairs or under the stairs. Small room, small budget.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;"><strong>Bought your own suite?</strong> Choose our labour-only refit, from £2,750. <strong>Not sure?</strong> We will tell you honestly at the free visit, even if the cheaper option is the right one.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How long does a bathroom installation take in Liverpool?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full bathroom usually takes 5 to 7 working days. A bath to shower conversion takes 2 to 3 days.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Free home visit (about 45 minutes).</strong> We measure the room and check where the pipes and waste run. Moving a waste is what turns a simple job into a costly one.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed written price.</strong> The full spec, written down. What is included is listed, and so is what is not. Change it before you commit.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 1: strip-out.</strong> The old bathroom comes out and leaves with us.</li>
        <li><strong>Days 1 to 3: first fix.</strong> New pipes and waste go in. Our partner electricians do any wiring. If we find rot or a leak, we show you and price it first.</li>
        <li><strong>Days 3 to 5: walls and floor.</strong> Boarding, waterproofing and tiling, or wall panels.</li>
        <li><strong>Final days: fit and hand over.</strong> The suite goes in. We test every joint, seal it all and clean the room.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Bigger rooms, a lot of tiling or moving the layout take longer. Your quote gives you the dates.</p>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Want a price for your bathroom?</strong> Book a free home visit. No pressure to book.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="bath-to-shower">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does it cost to replace a bath with a shower?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">From £2,395 including VAT, and it takes 2 to 3 days. It is the job we are asked for most.</p>
      <h3>What the job involves</h3>
      <p>The bath comes out first. The old taps and waste are capped or moved. This is where problems show up. A bath that has been in for 20 years often hides a rotten floorboard or a weeping waste. We check, and tell you what we find.</p>
      <p>Then the tray is set level, the valve goes in and the walls are finished. The enclosure goes on and we test it all.</p>
      <h3>Check your water system first</h3>
      <p>A shower that is wrong for your water system will dribble, however good it is. A combi, a tank in the loft and an unvented cylinder all behave in different ways. We check what you have and match the valve to it. Already bought a shower? We will tell you honestly if it will work.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="tiles">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Are tiles or wall panels better?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Tiles give more choice and suit most homes. Panels are quicker, usually cheaper, and have no grout to clean. We fit both.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>Tiles</th><th>Wall panels</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Cost</strong></td><td>Higher</td><td>Usually lower</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Time to fit</strong></td><td>Longer</td><td>Quicker</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Grout to clean</strong></td><td>Yes</td><td>None</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Choice of look</strong></td><td>Almost endless</td><td>Limited to the ranges</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Fixing damage later</strong></td><td>Swap a single tile</td><td>Often a whole panel</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>For a busy family bathroom or a rental, panels make a lot of sense. For a period home or a main bathroom you want to impress buyers with, tiles are usually worth it. We will say which we would pick for your room.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="access">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you fit a walk-in or accessible shower?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. We fit low level shower trays, grab rails and raised toilet seats. A low tray makes the step in much smaller.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>Swap a bath for a low level shower, from £2,395</li>
        <li>Thermostatic valve to guard against scalding</li>
        <li>Grab rails where you need them</li>
        <li>Raised toilet seats</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This is the most common change we make for people who struggle to get in and out of the bath. Call <a href="tel:01515580334">{PHONE}</a> and we will talk it through.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="why">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Why choose us as your bathroom fitters?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">One team for plumbing and tiling, a fixed price in writing, and a 12-month guarantee on our work.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <figure class="sg-photo">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-480.webp 480w, /images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 400px" />
            <img src="/images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-960.jpg" alt="New bath and shower fitted in a Liverpool bathroom" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </picture>
          <figcaption>A real job: new bath and shower fitted.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="sg-photo">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-480.webp 480w, /images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 400px" />
            <img src="/images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-960.jpg" alt="Shower room fitted by our team" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </picture>
          <figcaption>A real job: shower room fitted.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Fixed price in writing.</strong> If we find something behind the old bath, we price it before we touch it.</li>
        <li><strong>One team.</strong> Plumbing and tiling by James's team. Electrics booked in with our partner firm.</li>
        <li><strong>Guaranteed.</strong> 12 months on our work, and £2 million public liability insurance.</li>
        <li><strong>Tidy.</strong> We clean up and take all the rubbish away with us.</li>
        <li><strong>Emergency plumbers too.</strong> If anything goes wrong later, you call a firm that answers out of hours.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
